# The canonical constitution is sealed under a SHA-256 over its exact bytes.
#
# This repository runs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on
# checkout. Applied to a hash-sealed artifact that silently changes its bytes
# between commit and working tree, so a fresh clone would fail the integrity
# gate and the gate would report SUBJECT_INVALID -- accusing a corpus that
# nobody touched, and sending a reader to investigate the wrong thing.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths. The bytes that
# were sealed are the bytes that come back, on every platform.
#
# Do not "tidy" this by removing the attribute: the seal is only meaningful if
# the byte stream is stable, and the failure it prevents appears on someone
# else's machine rather than on the machine that removes it.

constitution.raw.md -text
seal.json           -text
